ne phosphatase suggests bone turnover", "Malignancy with bone metastases: weight loss and hypercalcemia consistent with this pattern", "Reactive leukocytosis from chronic stress/anxiety: normal differential but high WBC requires further distinction"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Leukocytosis"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.10576169624337406, "posterior": 0.06510351458819523, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The lack of blasts in the peripheral blood smear and normal differential weakly suggest against myeloid neoplasms with blasts, but further testing is needed fo…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.052, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The normal leukocyte differential reduces the likelihood of lymphoproliferative or plasma cell disorders, as these often present with specific cytopenias or bl…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4579481447338097, "posterior": 0.2818982181668854, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["CML typically presents with splenomegaly; its absence slightly reduces the likelihood of this diagnosis, though other features like elevated LAP remain relevan…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.20338787739110395, "posterior": 0.25039813303152014, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Hypercalcemia with weight loss and fatigue is a classic presentation of plasma cell disorders such as multiple myeloma, though normal leukocyte differential ma…"], "evidence_against": ["The normal leukocyte differential reduces the likelihood of lymphoproliferative or plasma cell disorders, as these often present with specific cytopenias or bl…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.22844526388568795, "posterior": 0.33749661962520405, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Reactive leukocytosis is supported by the normal differential and elevated LAP during recovery from a recent infection, though hypercalcemia complicates this i…"], "evidence_against": ["Hypercalcemia without concurrent infection or inflammation weakly contradicts reactive leukocytosis, which typically has metabolic causes rather than calcium d…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Metastatic Malignancy with Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT"